  data:  # ead8
    kind: invariant  # ead8
    title: "META: a multi-writer meta slot silently erases earlier writers; last-writer-wins has recurred 6 times with no mechanism"  # ead8
    status: violated  # ead8
    priority: 1  # ead8
    parent:  # ead8
    tags:  # ead8
    - analysis_quality  # ead8
    - dataflow  # ead8
    isbefore: []  # ead8
    duplicate_of: []  # ead8
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ead8
    pr_ref:  # ead8
    description: "## The class\n\nSix instances in four months, all one shape: **a meta slot that several\nwriters can reach holds a single value, so the last writer silently erases\nevery earlier one.** Each was fixed on its own, at its own call site, with a\nbespoke remedy. No mechanism prevents the seventh.\n\n| instance | slot | remedy shipped |\n|---|---|---|\n| INV-forim (2026-04-10) | edge.meta wholesale, 4 polyglot linkers | 4 point fixes + 4 per-linker regression tests |\n| BUG-04/05 family | single-value bare-name symbol dict | SymbolByName shared index (WI-sofaf) |\n| INV-zumin (2026-08-13) | edge.meta io_boundary, row order decided the winner | simultaneous marker in YAML |\n| INV-pojib (2026-08-13) | sanitizer registry slot | keyed registry |\n| INV-virat (2026-08-13) | edge.meta io_boundary, catalogue row erased the producer stamp | assign changed to append, stamp stays primary |\n| the caveat list (2026-08-13) | verify_claims caveats | _merge_caveat, folds by kind, keeps the union |\n\nTwo of the six were caught only by luck rather than by a test.\n\nINV-virat's own closure records that the INV-larol safety gate survived the\ndefect ONLY because the gate reads raw_edges while the tagger mutates an\naccidental shallow copy. A safety property resting on an accidental copy is\nnot a safety property.\n\nAnd INV-forim is in the same position TODAY. Nine sites in packages/*/src\nstill assign a whole fresh dict to .meta immediately after constructing the\nobject. None of the nine currently pass dataflow kwargs to Edge.create, and\nEdge.create leaves meta as None when no dataflow kwarg is given, so nothing\nis destroyed right now. That is safety by coincidence of which kwargs those\nnine call sites happen to use. Adding one access_mode= to any of them\nreinstates INV-forim in full, and no test fails.\n\n## Why the existing machinery does not catch it\n\naxis_meta_keys.py is a real registry: 84 keys, each declaring name, axis and\ndescription, with 27 property tests and ADR-0024 behind it. It is the right\nplace for this and it does not have it.\n\n1. **MetaKeySpec declares no arity.** Its fields are name, axis, description\n   and applicable_edge_types. Nothing anywhere records that a key has several\n   writers and therefore must be merged rather than assigned. The registry\n   polices WHICH keys may exist and WHAT vocabulary their values draw from.\n   It is blind to HOW MANY writers reach a key, by construction. A finished\n   conformance linter would have waved INV-virat straight through, because\n   the offending write is a correctly spelled assignment of a registered key.\n\n2. **The conformance linter does not exist.** The registry's own module\n   docstring says so: a subscript-access drift linter is a follow-on work\n   item, and the registry without the linter is already useful as the\n   canonical vocabulary for documentation. The 27 tests assert registry\n   well-formedness (no duplicate names, valid axis, non-empty description,\n   frozen dataclass, no collision with a typed field), not producer\n   conformance. The follow-on is WI-vusot, still todo_hard at priority 4.\n\n3. **Two of the four io keys are unregistered.** io_primitive and io_boundary\n   are registered (positional args, which is what made a name= grep miss\n   them). io_boundaries and io_mode are not in the 84.\n\n## Measured population\n\nInstrument walks the AST of every .py under packages/*/src and records four\nwrite shapes: subscript assignment, whole-dict assignment to .meta, a meta=\ndict literal passed to a constructor, and .update / .setdefault.\n\n- 275 distinct meta keys are written somewhere in src\n- 198 of those are not in the 84-key registry\n- 80 keys are written by more than one module\n\nModule count is NOT collision count and must not be reported as one. A key\nwritten by 26 linkers that each construct their own edges has 26 writers and\nzero collisions. The dangerous shape is narrower: a key written at\nconstruction AND also written post-hoc by a pass that walks edges it did not\ncreate. That is exactly the io_boundary tagger, and it is what both August\ninstances were.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nExtend the existing registry rather than adding a parallel mechanism.\n\n1. A required write_discipline field on MetaKeySpec, no default, one of\n   single_writer, merge_union, producer_primary, unaudited. A property test\n   asserts every spec declares one, so a new key cannot be added without an\n   answer.\n\n2. unaudited is a first-class state, not an omission. Declaring\n   single_writer wrongly buys a FALSE assurance, which is worse than no\n   assurance. The count of unaudited keys is reported as visible debt rather\n   than hidden behind a permissive default.\n\n3. A chokepoint writer that enforces the declared discipline at runtime:\n   merge_union folds by key and keeps the union, producer_primary refuses to\n   let a later writer displace a producer stamp.\n\n4. A static check plus CI test that fails when a key declared merge_union or\n   producer_primary is assigned directly rather than through the chokepoint,\n   and when a whole fresh dict is assigned to .meta on a just-constructed\n   object (the INV-forim shape).\n\n5. Register io_boundaries and io_mode, and declare disciplines for the io\n   family, so the two August instances become mechanically impossible rather\n   than fixed-in-place.\n\nScope note, stated rather than hidden: this does NOT audit all 84 keys. It\nlands the mechanism, declares the keys where there is evidence, and leaves\nthe rest explicitly unaudited with a count."  # ead8
    fields:  # ead8
      statement: "A meta key reachable by more than one writer must declare its write discipline in axis_meta_keys.py, and a later writer must not be able to silently erase an earlier writer value."  # ead8
      root_cause: "MetaKeySpec declares name, axis, description and applicable_edge_types but no arity or write discipline, and the registry conformance linter it names as a follow-on (WI-vusot, todo_hard P4) was never built. So the registry polices which keys may exist and what vocabulary their values draw from, and is structurally blind to how many writers reach a key. Six instances of last-writer-wins on a shared slot were each fixed at their own call site with a bespoke remedy; nothing prevents the seventh."  # ead8
